# The Project Graph's concept scheme: the vocabulary its comment tags point at.
#
# PROVISIONAL, from stage 3a. It holds one concept only, so the plumbing has something to check.
# Stage 3b replaces it with the pilot's concept list, which is Andy's to decide: which concepts,
# their labels, their hierarchy, and how the homonyms in docs/project-graph/inventory.md split.
#
# The scheme's IRI is the document's own, with no fragment, and each concept is a fragment of it,
# the usual pattern for a hash namespace. See docs/project-graph/id-design.md.

@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix concept: <https://andyfitzgeraldconsulting.com/ns/project-graph/concepts#> .

<https://andyfitzgeraldconsulting.com/ns/project-graph/concepts>
  a skos:ConceptScheme .

concept:focus-ring
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://andyfitzgeraldconsulting.com/ns/project-graph/concepts> ;
  skos:prefLabel "focus ring"@en .
